s to recycle these  containers and other locally found  materials  it was something that was helping us to  be more eco-friendly we were cautious of  how much land we're using we didn't want  to go into the bush and clear land and  destroy the forest we wanted to be  cautious about how much water we were  using we didn't want to keep irrigating  the soil and then it just runs off and  then we have to get more water we wanted  to be able to make sure that we're  increasing our yield practie the idea  behind this is to bring fresh quality  produce directly to those who need it  they harvest at least a hundred and  twenty kilograms a month so far eighty  eight companies buy the veggies in large  quantities some individuals order as  well  Food Security poverty and migration are  persistent problems in Nigeria I really  just want to improve my country and add  to my country if I could be using my  brain there I can be using my brain here  so the concept is how do we develop our  own spaces how do we make sure that our  own people have jobs we're not gonna  wait for government to do it we're not  gonna wait for anybody to do it we're  gonna do it ourselves  in the mean time at Elijah has moved on  to the next generation in vertical  farming technology she wants to make  agriculture more attractive to Nigeria's  young people
 

